% The Ponens policies do-178c-software-assurance, as a program of Logical English for LPS.
%
% Written by lpsPlus's ponens_twin.pl (docs/migration/ponens.md) from 19
% Ponens policies, whose files are in sources/ (Ponens: github.com/imandra-ai/
% ponens, MIT licence), with 2 Ponens traces as its scenarios.
%
% Each step of a trace is an action of the session Ponens recorded. Each
% policy is a causal law that records a breach: at the step where the policy
% fails, when the step ends, or at the end of the session when the policy
% looks forward. Where a scenario has a comment above it, the comment is what
% Ponens's own evaluator (`ponens trace check --json`) says of the same
% policies on that trace.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from the policies of
% another system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
% express or implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or
% fit for a particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against
% its source before relying on it. It is not legal, regulatory or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 24.

the events are:
    step *a step* is a *a kind*; known as step_is_a.
    step *a step* shows *a sign*; known as step_shows.
    step *a step* comes after step *an other step* in its chain; known as chain_link.
    step *a step* comes after step *an other step* on its target; known as target_link.
    step *a step* ends; known as step_ends.
    the trace shows *a sign*; known as trace_shows.
    artifact *an artifact* is made by step *a step*; known as made_by_event.
    artifact *an artifact* is a *a kind* artifact; known as artifact_kind_event.
    artifact *an artifact* derives from artifact *an other artifact*; known as derives_event.
    the session ends; known as session_ends.

the fluents are:
    step *a step* was a *a kind*; known as was_a.
    step *a step* has shown *a sign*; known as has_shown.
    step *a step* is in the chain of step *an other step*; known as in_chain.
    step *a step* shares a target with step *an other step*; known as shares_target.
    step *a step* has ended; known as has_ended.
    the trace has shown *a sign*; known as trace_has_shown.
    artifact *an artifact* was made by step *a step*; known as made_by.
    artifact *an artifact* was a *a kind* artifact; known as artifact_kind.
    artifact *an artifact* derived from artifact *an other artifact*; known as derived.
    step *a step* meets *a condition*; known as meets.
    the trace meets *a condition*; known as trace_meets.
    the policy *a policy* is broken at step *a step*; known as broken_at.
    the policy *a policy* is broken; known as broken.

the knowledge base do 178c software assurance includes:

% What a trace records, kept to the end of the session.
when step a step is a a kind
then step the step was a the kind.

when step a step shows a sign
then step the step has shown the sign.

when step a step comes after step an other step in its chain
then step the other step is in the chain of step the step.

when step a step comes after step an other step on its target
then step the other step shares a target with step the step.

when step a step ends
then step the step has ended.

when the trace shows a sign
then the trace has shown the sign.

when artifact an artifact is made by step a step
then artifact the artifact was made by step the step.

when artifact an artifact is a a kind artifact
then artifact the artifact was a the kind artifact.

when artifact an artifact derives from artifact an other artifact
then artifact the artifact derived from artifact the other artifact.

% accomplishment_summary (error): F(AccomplishmentSummary)
% DO-178C Table A-10 obj 3: the means of compliance and evidence are provided to the certification authority, summarised in the Software Accomplishment Summary.
the trace meets "some step is a AccomplishmentSummary" at a time if
    step a step has ended at the time
    and step the step was a AccomplishmentSummary at the time.

when the session ends
    and it is not the case that the trace meets "some step is a AccomplishmentSummary"
then the policy accomplishment_summary is broken.

% artifacts_baselined (error): G((HLR ∨ LLR ∨ SourceCode ∨ Test) → baselined)
% DO-178C Table A-8: configuration items are identified, baselines established, and the integrity of the configuration is maintained throughout the life cycle.
step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR" at a time if
    step the step was a "HLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR" at a time if
    step the step was a "LLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode" at a time if
    step the step was a SourceCode at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode or is a Test" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode or is a Test" at a time if
    step the step was a Test at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode or is a Test"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "baselined"
then the policy artifacts_baselined is broken at step the step.

% changes_controlled (error): G(Change → P(change_approved))
% DO-178C Table A-8: problem reporting, change control, change review and configuration status accounting govern any modification to baselined data.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows change approved" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "change approved" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Change
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows change approved"
then the policy changes_controlled is broken at step the step.

% code_trace_to_llr (error): G(SourceCode → P_chain(LLR))
% DO-178C Table A-2 obj 6 & A-5 obj 5: source code is developed from low-level requirements; traceability is established through the artifact lineage.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a LLR" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a "LLR" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a SourceCode
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a LLR"
then the policy code_trace_to_llr is broken at step the step.

% code_verified (error): G(SourceCode → reviewed ∨ analyzed)
% DO-178C Table A-5: source code is verified for compliance, accuracy, and conformance to standards before integration. Not required at DAL D.
step a step meets "shows reviewed or shows analyzed" at a time if
    step the step has shown "reviewed" at the time.

step a step meets "shows reviewed or shows analyzed" at a time if
    step the step has shown "analyzed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a SourceCode
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows reviewed or shows analyzed"
then the policy code_verified is broken at step the step.

% derived_requirements_to_safety (error): G(DerivedRequirement → P(safety_assessed))
% DO-178C §5.1.2 / Tables A-2: derived requirements are defined and provided to the system processes, including the system safety assessment, so their impact is evaluated.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows safety assessed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "safety assessed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a DerivedRequirement
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows safety assessed"
then the policy derived_requirements_to_safety is broken at step the step.

% hlr_trace_to_system (error): G(HLR → P_chain(SystemRequirement))
% DO-178C Table A-2 obj 1 & A-3 obj 6: high-level requirements are developed from system requirements; traceability is established through the artifact lineage.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a SystemRequirement" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a SystemRequirement at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a "HLR"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a SystemRequirement"
then the policy hlr_trace_to_system is broken at step the step.

% hlr_verified (error): G(HLR → reviewed ∧ requirements_accurate)
% DO-178C Table A-3: HLR are verified for compliance with system requirements, accuracy, consistency, verifiability and conformance to standards.
step a step meets "shows reviewed and shows requirements accurate" at a time if
    step the step has shown "reviewed" at the time
    and step the step has shown "requirements accurate" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a "HLR"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "shows reviewed and shows requirements accurate"
then the policy hlr_verified is broken at step the step.

% llr_trace_to_hlr (error): G(LLR → P_chain(HLR))
% DO-178C Table A-2 obj 4-5 & A-4 obj 6: low-level requirements and architecture are developed from high-level requirements, traceable through the lineage.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a HLR" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a "HLR" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a "LLR"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a HLR"
then the policy llr_trace_to_hlr is broken at step the step.

% llr_verified (error): G(LLR → reviewed)
% DO-178C Table A-4: low-level requirements and software architecture are verified for compliance, accuracy and consistency. Reviews of design are not required at DAL D.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a "LLR"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "reviewed"
then the policy llr_verified is broken at step the step.

% plans_before_development (error): G((HLR ∨ LLR ∨ SourceCode) → P(plans_approved))
% DO-178C Table A-1: the software planning process produces the software plans and standards that govern development and verification; these must precede development.
step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a "HLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a "LLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (2)" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (2)" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (2)" at a time if
    step the step was a SourceCode at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step shows plans approved" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "plans approved" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (2)"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows plans approved"
then the policy plans_before_development is broken at step the step.

% problem_reports_closed (warning): G(ProblemReport → F(resolved ∨ deferred_with_rationale))
% DO-178C Table A-8 / §7.2.3: problem reporting records process non-compliances and product deficiencies, which are tracked to resolution or documented deferral.
step a step meets "shows resolved or shows deferred with rationale" at a time if
    step the step has shown "resolved" at the time.

step a step meets "shows resolved or shows deferred with rationale" at a time if
    step the step has shown "deferred with rationale" at the time.

step a step meets "it or a later step shows resolved or shows deferred with rationale" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step meets "shows resolved or shows deferred with rationale" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a ProblemReport
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step shows resolved or shows deferred with rationale"
then the policy problem_reports_closed is broken at step the step.

% psac_agreed (error): G((HLR ∨ LLR ∨ SourceCode) → P(psac_agreed))
% DO-178C Table A-10 obj 1: communication and understanding between the applicant and the certification authority is established via the PSAC. Table A-10 applies at Levels A-D.
step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (3)" at a time if
    step the step was a "HLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (3)" at a time if
    step the step was a "LLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (3)" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (3)" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (3)" at a time if
    step the step was a SourceCode at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step shows psac agreed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "psac agreed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (3)"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows psac agreed"
then the policy psac_agreed is broken at step the step.

% sqa_conformity (error): G((HLR ∨ LLR ∨ SourceCode) → sqa_reviewed)
% DO-178C Table A-9: SQA obtains assurance that the software life-cycle processes comply with approved plans and standards, and conducts a software conformity review.
step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (4)" at a time if
    step the step was a "HLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (4)" at a time if
    step the step was a "LLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (4)" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (4)" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (4)" at a time if
    step the step was a SourceCode at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (4)"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "sqa reviewed"
then the policy sqa_conformity is broken at step the step.

% standards_defined (error): G(SourceCode → P(standards_defined))
% DO-178C Table A-1 obj 6-7: requirements, design and code standards are defined so outputs can be checked for conformance. Not required at DAL D.
step a step meets "an earlier step shows standards defined" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step has shown "standards defined" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a SourceCode
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step shows standards defined"
then the policy standards_defined is broken at step the step.

% structural_coverage_achieved (error): G(CoverageAnalysis → coverage_achieved)
% DO-178C Table A-7 obj 5-8: structural coverage is analysed — modified condition/decision coverage at DAL A, decision coverage at B, statement coverage at C. No structural coverage objective at DAL D.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a CoverageAnalysis
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "coverage achieved"
then the policy structural_coverage_achieved is broken at step the step.

% test_traces_to_requirement (error): G(Test → P_chain(HLR))
% DO-178C Table A-7 obj 1-2: test cases trace to requirements and requirements trace to test cases, ensuring complete coverage of requirements by tests.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a HLR (2)" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a "HLR" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Test
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a HLR (2)"
then the policy test_traces_to_requirement is broken at step the step.

% tests_requirements_based (error): G(Test → requirements_based)
% DO-178C Table A-6: test cases and procedures are developed from the high- and low-level requirements; testing is requirements-based.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Test
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "requirements based"
then the policy tests_requirements_based is broken at step the step.

% verification_independent (warning): G((HLR ∨ LLR ∨ SourceCode) ∧ dal_a → independent_review)
% DO-178C Annex A 'with independence' columns: a number of verification objectives must be satisfied with independence at Levels A and B.
step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (5)" at a time if
    step the step was a "HLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (5)" at a time if
    step the step was a "LLR" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (5)" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR (5)" at the time.

step a step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (5)" at a time if
    step the step was a SourceCode at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step meets "is a HLR or is a LLR or is a SourceCode (5)"
    and step the step has shown "dal a"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "independent review"
then the policy verification_independent is broken at step the step.

scenario governed is:
    % Ponens: every policy of the pack passes on this trace.
    artifact code1 is made by step 5 from 1 to 2.
    artifact hlr1 is made by step 3 from 1 to 2.
    artifact llr1 is made by step 4 from 1 to 2.
    artifact sys1 is made by step 2 from 1 to 2.
    artifact test1 is made by step 6 from 1 to 2.
    artifact sys1 is a SystemRequirement artifact from 1 to 2.
    artifact hlr1 is a "HLR" artifact from 1 to 2.
    artifact llr1 is a "LLR" artifact from 1 to 2.
    artifact code1 is a SourceCode artifact from 1 to 2.
    artifact test1 is a Test artifact from 1 to 2.
    artifact hlr1 derives from artifact sys1 from 1 to 2.
    artifact llr1 derives from artifact hlr1 from 1 to 2.
    artifact code1 derives from artifact llr1 from 1 to 2.
